    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16590" root="رمث" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَمِثٌ</span></b>  [part. n. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَمِثَ</span>]. You say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِبِلٌ رَمِثَةٌ</span>, (S,
M, K,) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَمَاثَى</span> (S, K) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَمْثَى</span>, (M, K,)
[which are pls.,] <i>Camels having a complaint from
eating</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رِمْث</span>. (S, M, K. [See 1, third sentence.])

